<title>UK: UK reserves rise underlying $7.0 mln in October.</title>
<headline>UK reserves rise underlying $7.0 mln in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's gold and currency reserves rose an underlying $7.0 million in October, the Treasury said. (IN MLN DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>				     October		September</p>
<p> Underlying reserves	  + 7.0		    - 113</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had expected a rise in the region of $50 Million.  </p>
<p>    Overall reserves	  + 2,610		  -3,878</p>
<p>    Total			 46.69 billion	  44.08 billion</p>
<p>The underlying change excludes factors included in the total change (IN MLN OF DOLLARS EXCEPT WHERE STATED)</p>
<p>					    October	    September</p>
<p> Ecu Treasury bill proceeds     + 1,268		+ 1,268</p>
<p> Ecu Treasury bills maturing    - 1,267		- 1,268</p>
<p>Repayments under the  exchange cover scheme (ECS)    - 10		   - 8</p>
<p> Privatisation receipts	     --		   - 148</p>
<p>Proceeds from issued $2bln FRN +1,992 HMG debt assigned from public</p>
<p>    sector			    -13			--</p>
<p> Revaluation of EMI swap	  -19			--</p>
<p> Total of adjustments	     +2,610		 - 3,878</p>
<p> Underlying change		  + 7.0		  - 113</p>
</text>
